diff --git a/docs/DELEGATION_EFFICIENCY_EVENT_CONTRACT.md b/docs/DELEGATION_EFFICIENCY_EVENT_CONTRACT.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..8df7d3b14
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/DELEGATION_EFFICIENCY_EVENT_CONTRACT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+# Delegation efficiency event contract
+
+This document is the human-readable companion to the machine-readable
+inventory in `jcode_app_core::measurement`. It is a runtime input contract,
+not a persistence or reporting design.
+
+## Versions and compatibility
+
+- `envelope`: `jcode.delegation-efficiency.v1` identifies this contract family.
+- `schema_version`: `1.0` identifies serialized field names, units, and types.
+- `semantics_version`: `part1-runtime-1` identifies field meaning and evidence.
+- A consumer must reject a different schema or semantics version.
+- The schema is closed. Unknown fields, including arbitrary `x_*` fields, are
+  rejected before detached delivery and persistence.
+- Unknown event kinds are rejected and are never silently coerced.
+
+## Event inventory
+
+| Event kind | Meaning | Required identity | Main nullable facts |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `tool_attempt` | An invocation reached policy, resolution, or execution. | event, session, tool invocation | guard, outcome details |
+| `tool_result` | A successful or failed tool result reached the measurement boundary. | event, session, tool invocation | guard, measurements, transform |
+| `provider_usage` | Provider-reported usage at a response boundary. | event, session, attribution status | request, generation, attempt, response facts, cost |
+| `delegation_spawn` | A point event for a spawned specialized session. | event, parent and child when known | delegation, guard, blueprint |
+| `delegation_follow_up` | A point event for a paginated follow-up. | event, parent and child when known | delegation and guard |
+| `delegation_summary` | A point event for a summary request. | event, parent and child when known | delegation and guard |
+| `child_session` | A child-session provenance point event. | event, parent and child when known | delegation and guard |
+| `observer_health` | Content-free detached observer health fact. | event and time | all operation facts |
+
+All byte fields are bytes, line fields are lines, token fields are counts,
+latencies are milliseconds, monetary fields are provider response amounts in
+micro-units, and timestamps are UTC Unix milliseconds. `chars_div_4` is an
+approximation, not a model tokenizer. `measured`, `estimated`,
+`provider_reported`, and `unknown` evidence labels must not be conflated.
+
+## Null, unknown, and not applicable
+
+Fields are serialized as `null` when the fact is not supplied or does not apply
+to the event. `unknown` is a bounded classification for an observed unknown
+state, not a substitute identifier. Absence is reserved for additive fields
+that are not part of the current serialized envelope. Missing provider request,
+generation, or attempt identities are unknown linkage and must not be joined
+using timing, model, event order, text, or child-session identity. jcode-issued
+provider request events carry explicit request and generation IDs plus an
+attempt number. A provider path that cannot supply or preserve those fields is
+serialized as `unknown_linkage` and remains unattributed.
+
+OpenRouter-family response facts preserve response ID, served model, route,
+timestamp, total cost, cache classes, and exposed cost components. The runtime
+does not fabricate currency. Missing cost remains nullable and no provider
+outside this family receives a local price estimate. Response-time cost is
+immutable provider-reported source evidence, not billing truth. A future
+reconciliation must be a separate derived record and must not rewrite it.
+
+## Privacy and bounds
+
+The structural allowlist accepts only scalar fields in the inventory. Unknown
+fields, including `x_*` extensions, are rejected. IDs are at most 128 bytes and
+contain only ASCII letters, digits, `.`, `_`, `:`, and `-`. Other strings are at
+most 256 bytes and cannot contain control characters. Timestamps are bounded to
+the range from Unix epoch through year 2100. The complete serialized envelope
+is at most 16 KiB. Nested objects, arrays, prompts, arguments, results,
+summaries, paths, hashes, and arbitrary metadata are rejected before detached
+delivery.
+
+## Local identifier access and retention boundary
+
+Event IDs, session IDs, tool invocation IDs, guard IDs, delegation IDs, and
+provider response IDs are local-detail join keys. Their purpose is point-event
+debugging and explicit provenance joins, not user profiling or billing.
+They may cross only the configured local `delegation_efficiency` observer
+boundary and must not be sent to hosted telemetry. Access is limited to the
+local jcode process and an explicitly configured local observer command. The
+runtime does not retain them, write a database, or create a queue. Consequently
+the runtime's retention period is zero: once the detached observer receives an
+event, retention and deletion are the observer/plugin's responsibility and
+must be documented and enforced before Part 2 persistence. jcode provides no
+local-detail export or recovery operation.
